PATCH 306: register + reconstruct the phase-0x1c render-script handler 0x41c7 and its callee dd15 =
the per-frame CAMERA -> extender-TCB copy (the LIVE mission camera feed the op-0x24 9200 voxel
renderer needs).  asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin (DS=DGROUP=0x1c00).

The in-mission 22dd render-cursor-walk dispatches the phase-0x1c script @DGROUP:0x6c82 =
[23ef,41c7,2471,286e,3b59,23ce,...] via `call word[DGROUP:cursor]`.  Script entry 1 = 0x41c7, an
UNPROMOTED engine mid-entry (Ghidra never recovered it -> the fist_icall fmap TRAPPED it -> the
handler's own `addw $2,[0x4a86]` cursor-advance never ran -> the 22dd loop SPUN FOREVER -> 459a never
completed the frame -> the 209e paint walk / op-0x24 poster was never reached).  This was the pinned
frontier (gdb-verified spin at 0x2471=off 9329 dispatch, cursor stuck at entry 1).

  FUN_0000_41c7 (asm 0x41c7): `call dd15; addw $2,[0x4a86]; ret` -- feed the camera, advance the cursor.
  FUN_0000_dd15 (asm 0xdd15-0xddc3): structurally identical to db99 (patch 193) -- ddff() builds the
    viewport geom record into the extender TCB (es:di = word[0xea2e]:word[0xea2c] = DAT_2000_aa2c), then
    the mission camera block DGROUP:0x155a (= d548+0x12, the SAME source db99 copies) is written to
    rec+0x2c..0x36 (32-bit X/Y/Z), rec+0x38/0x3e/0x3c/0x3a (heading/detail from the word[0x6d34]
    descriptor + byte[0x154a]), and extender op 8 (display-list setup) is posted via e339.  Base-loss
    rebase: every si/bx near-offset -> g_mem+0x1c000+off; TCB = DAT_2000_aa2c (patch 068).  The +0x3f2
    inbox EBX low16 = the sar-computed value (high16 caller-ambient, op-8 handler overwrites it per the
    op-0xc/db99 precedent -> not fabricated).

Both are registered in the fist_icall fmap (the unpromoted-mid-entry class, patches 121/193/292).
OBSERVED-REACHED on the genuine BATTLES(160,100)->OK(205,128)->ACCEPT(40,186) AZER1 run: op 0x08 now
POSTS and the cursor advances past 41c7 to entry 2 (0x2471, the next frontier -> patch 307).
MISSION-PATH ONLY (the 22dd interpreter is gated by byte[DGROUP:0x1548] d548 > 0, which is 0 on the
menu + every one of the 19 verify flows) -> strictly behaviour-neutral (verify.sh both = 19/19).

